ArjunaOS Manifest
=================

This repository is the manifest entry point for **ArjunaOS**.

Right now it is still heavily based on the LineageOS manifest structure on branch `lineage-23.2`. That is intentional. ArjunaOS is being built as a live tutorial series, so this repo will stay close to upstream first and then grow its own manifest entries as the articles move forward.

Getting started
---------------

To initialize a local ArjunaOS workspace, run:

```
repo init -u https://github.com/AOSPInsider/android.git -b lineage-23.2 --git-lfs
```

Then sync the source tree:

```
repo sync
```

At this stage, most projects in the workspace still come from upstream LineageOS and AOSP. ArjunaOS-specific repositories will be added here only when the tutorial reaches the point where they are needed.

What this repo is for
---------------------

- owning the manifest entry point for ArjunaOS from day one
- keeping the tutorial flow reproducible
- adding ArjunaOS-specific repos gradually instead of inventing them too early
- keeping the relationship with upstream LineageOS clear

Notes
-----

- This repo is not the full source tree. It is the manifest repo that tells `repo` what to sync.
- The current branch tracks the `lineage-23.2` base.
- If you are following the tutorial, use this manifest repo even before ArjunaOS-specific repos exist.

Contributing
------------

For now, changes here should stay focused on manifest and source-layout work related to ArjunaOS.
